==Indonesian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|id|ms|kemarin}}, {{m|ms|kelmarin}}, from {{inh|id|ms-cla|کمارين|tr=kemarin}}, {{m|ms-cla|کلمارين|tr=kelmarin}}, from {{inh|id|poz-mly-pro|*kə maləm hari(-an)}}. Equivalent to {{blend|id|ke|malam|hari|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|id|[kəˈmarɪn]}}
* {{audio|id|LL-Q9240 (ind)-Xbypass-kemarin.wav}}
* {{hyphenation|id|kê|ma|rin}}

===Noun===
{{id-noun|head=kêmarin|pl=-}}

# [[yesterday]]:
## the day immediately before today; one day ago
## the recent past

===Adverb===
{{head|id|adverb|head=kêmarin}}

# [[yesterday]]: on the day before today
#: {{ant|id|besok}}
#: {{uxi|id|'''Kemarin''' [[aku]] [[pergi]] [[ke]] [[rumah]] [[teman]].|I was going to a friend's home '''yesterday'''.}}
# [[recently]]: in the recent past

